{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandatory unbiased political education in schools",
        "additional_details": "This should be delivered by an unbiased teacher or specialist and delivered in separate lessons or in life skills lesson delivered by schools across a dedicated curriculum. This will prevent false news and parents or caregivers influence a young persons vote and allows them to formulate their own opinions. Schools can decide when they deliver these lessons however during election time special lessons to vote aged students should be delivered to refresh and remind them of the parties.",
        "background": "Implementation of a political curriculum to teach the younger generation how the system works. It should also give them insight into what political parties believe and what they stand for. This will benefit young voter turnout and should be delivered in a unbiased setting and manner.",
